<h2>Catechist's Guide</h2>
<p class="big-question">For class preparation and delivery. For the catechist's use only.</p>

<h3>Class Summary</h3>

<p><strong>Estimated duration:</strong> 60 minutes</p>
<p><strong>Central theme:</strong> God created the world out of nothing by love and governs it with his providence; evil does not contradict the goodness of God.</p>
<p><strong>Objectives:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Understand that God created everything out of nothing, not out of necessity but out of love.</li>
<li>Recognize that creation is a Trinitarian work: Father, Son, and Holy Spirit.</li>
<li>Internalize that God declared his creation &laquo;very good&raquo; and that matter is not evil.</li>
<li>Understand divine providence and how it relates to freedom and evil.</li>
<li>Trust that God sustains creation at every moment and brings good out of evil.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Key verse:</strong> &laquo;You love all things that exist, and you hate none of the things you have made, for you would not have made anything if you had hated it&raquo; (Wis 11:24)</p>
<p><strong>CCC references:</strong> 279-324</p>

</section>

