<section class="content">

<h3>Difficult Questions</h3>

<h4>&laquo;If God is good and all-powerful, why does he permit evil?&raquo;</h4>
<p>This is the oldest and most difficult question of faith. The Catechism does not offer an easy answer, but it teaches that God respects the freedom of his creatures and that from every evil he can bring a greater good (CCC 309-314). The cross is the definitive proof: from the worst crime in history, God brought the greatest salvation. It is not about understanding evil, but about trusting that God is present even in suffering.</p>

<h4>&laquo;Does science contradict creation?&raquo;</h4>
<p>No. Faith and science answer different questions. Science explains how; faith answers why and what for. The Genesis account is not a biology textbook, but a revelation about the origin and meaning of the world (CCC 283-289). Catholics can accept evolution as a scientific tool while affirming that God is the ultimate creator of everything.</p>

<h4>&laquo;Are angels real or are they symbols?&raquo;</h4>
<p>They are real. The Catechism teaches that angels are spiritual, personal, and immortal beings, created by God as &laquo;servants and messengers&raquo; of his plan of salvation (CCC 329-330). They are not pious ornaments or ancient myths. They actively participate in the history of salvation. But we should not fall into exaggerated angelology that distracts from Christ.</p>

<h4>&laquo;What does it mean that God &lsquo;sustains&rsquo; creation at every moment?&raquo;</h4>
<p>It means that creation is not a past event that God &laquo;left running.&raquo; Without God&rsquo;s continuous action, everything would return to nothing. &laquo;In him we live and move and have our being&raquo; (Acts 17:28). Your existence at this very second depends on God&rsquo;s creative love, not only on the love that acted at the beginning, but on the love that acts now (CCC 301).</p>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Catechist's Prayer</h3>

<blockquote>
<p>Lord, you who created the world out of nothing<br />
and sustain it with your love at every moment,<br />
give me the grace to transmit this truth with fire:<br />
that nothing exists by chance,<br />
that everything is a gift of your love,<br />
that evil does not have the last word.<br />
Help me to help others trust in your providence,<br />
even when they do not understand the path.<br />
May my life be a witness that you sustain all things.<br />
Amen.</p>
</blockquote>

